Chromium os_crypt cookie decryption (widely documented technique)

The Doubao source (backend/doubao_cookies.go, backend/doubao_dpapi_windows.go)
implements the standard Chromium-on-Windows cookie recovery used by many
open-source cookie readers: base64 `os_crypt.encrypted_key` from `Local State`
with a "DPAPI" prefix, unwrapped via CryptUnprotectData (CurrentUser) to a
32-byte AES key, then `v10`-framed cookie values decrypted as
nonce(12) | ciphertext | tag(16) with AES-256-GCM, skipping the 32-byte fixed
header. This is an independent implementation of a public technique; no third
party's source code was copied.

